<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hedwig Jagiellon, Duchess of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1457">1457</a>–<a href="/years/1502">1502</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hedwig Jagiellon was a Polish princess, a daughter of King Casimir IV, who married Duke George the Rich of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a> in 1475. Their wedding at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> was one of the most lavish festivities of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and is re-enacted every four years as the Landshut Wedding. She spent much of her later life at the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghausen">Burghausen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hedwig-jagiellon-duchess-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Hedwig Jagiellon, Duchess of Bavaria" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jadwiga_Jagiellonka.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
